# The languages Skwir offers (ADR-139, 13): Automatic speaks them, and the
# Language setting lists them by their names alone. Any other language a
# catalog is in is listed as incomplete, with its share, for whoever
# chooses it, and Automatic never picks it.
#
# One tag a line, as its catalogs are named (fr). `just words` adds a
# language once 90% of all Skwir's messages are translated and reviewed in
# it (a message is reviewed once the `# draft` above it is gone), and every
# message of what is on by default is: the program's own crates (core, the
# platform, the window, the host of plugins from outside) and each plugin
# on by default.
#
# Only a person takes one out, which lists it as incomplete again: a
# release refuses a language here with less than 75% of its messages
# reviewed (`just words --release`), while between releases it stays
# offered, what it lacks said in English. Its line comes back only once it
# meets the bar again.
